  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "25145826",
      "title": "Adding Static Site Generation (SSG) On The Home Page",
      "lectureOrder": 295,
      "videoOrder": 274,
      "sourceHash": "c5ce9cf4b9ed9091fc067e35d70a60eea3b4bb9db1b9323e4d596a96a6342158",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.09,
          "end": 4.86,
          "en": "Now let's start with the starting page.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.86,
          "end": 6.61,
          "en": "Here on this starting page,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 6.61,
          "end": 9.38,
          "en": "we want the featured events.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 9.38,
          "end": 12.1,
          "en": "So we need to load those featured events",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 12.1,
          "end": 14.34,
          "en": "onto this index.js page.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 14.34,
          "end": 16.6,
          "en": "So into this index.js component here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 16.6,
          "end": 18.63,
          "en": "this homepage component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 18.63,
          "end": 22.4,
          "en": "The question now is how do we wanna load the data?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 22.4,
          "end": 26.55,
          "en": "Now we could do it with client site data fetching.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 26.55,
          "end": 29.77,
          "en": "We could use useEffect with the fetch API",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 29.77,
          "end": 34.07,
          "en": "or install and use the useSWR hook here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 34.07,
          "end": 36.01,
          "en": "which we learned about.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 36.01,
          "end": 39.21,
          "en": "We could do that, but does this make sense?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 39.21,
          "end": 41.97,
          "en": "Is this the best solution here?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 41.97,
          "end": 45.13,
          "en": "I would argue that here we actually wanna use,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 45.13,
          "end": 48.79,
          "en": "one of the two forms of pre-rendering instead.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 48.79,
          "end": 52.74,
          "en": "So static generation or server-side rendering.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 52.74,
          "end": 56.41,
          "en": "Because the starting page, which we're looking at here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 56.41,
          "end": 59.07,
          "en": "this is a page which should be understood",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 59.07,
          "end": 61.12,
          "en": "by search engine crawlers.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 61.12,
          "end": 65.06,
          "en": "It's important that they are able to understand our site",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 65.06,
          "end": 68.31,
          "en": "and well, direct traffic to our site.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 68.31,
          "end": 71.65,
          "en": "And as a visitor on this page, it would also be nice",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 71.65,
          "end": 73.93,
          "en": "if we see something instantly.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 73.93,
          "end": 75.44,
          "en": "It's also not likely",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 75.44,
          "end": 79.05,
          "en": "that this data changes multiple times per second",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 79.05,
          "end": 80.25,
          "en": "or minute even.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 80.25,
          "end": 83.65,
          "en": "So there isn't really a reason for loading this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 83.65,
          "end": 85.08,
          "en": "on the client side.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 85.08,
          "end": 87.85,
          "en": "It's also not some user specific data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 87.85,
          "end": 91.31,
          "en": "and it's also not data behind a login screen",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 91.31,
          "end": 93.34,
          "en": "or anything like that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 93.34,
          "end": 96.03,
          "en": "So here I would argue, it makes a lot of sense",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 96.03,
          "end": 99.72,
          "en": "to pre-render this page with some data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 99.72,
          "end": 102.53,
          "en": "That then just leaves one question,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 102.53,
          "end": 104.13,
          "en": "should we use getServersideProps",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 105.44,
          "end": 109.7,
          "en": "for real server-side pre-rendering where the page",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 109.7,
          "end": 114.7,
          "en": "is pre-rendered on the server on the fly for every request",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 114.91,
          "end": 119.25,
          "en": "or do we want getStaticProps to pre-render the page,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 119.25,
          "end": 124.16,
          "en": "during the build process and potentially also on the server",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 124.16,
          "end": 127.04,
          "en": "if we set revalidate to a certain value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 127.04,
          "end": 131.63,
          "en": "so that we have a mostly updated page.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 131.63,
          "end": 133.35,
          "en": "I would argue for this kind of page,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 133.35,
          "end": 135.56,
          "en": "we don't need server-side rendering.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 135.56,
          "end": 138.97,
          "en": "We don't need to pre-render it for every request,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 138.97,
          "end": 143.12,
          "en": "instead using getStaticProps makes most sense here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 143.12,
          "end": 144.31,
          "en": "I would say.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 144.31,
          "end": 147.133,
          "en": "So we can export this async function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 147.133,
          "end": 152.133,
          "en": "getStaticProps here in this index.js file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 152.16,
          "end": 156.02,
          "en": "Get our context, though here, we won't need it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 156.02,
          "end": 157.69,
          "en": "So we can also omit it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 157.69,
          "end": 158.82999999999998,
          "en": "And then in here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 158.82999999999998,
          "end": 163.82999999999998,
          "en": "return an object with the props for this homepage component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 165,
          "end": 166.69,
          "en": "Now the props should be an object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 166.69,
          "end": 171.69,
          "en": "and in there I want to have my featured events",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 171.8,
          "end": 174.39,
          "en": "which now should be fetched from Firebase,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 174.39,
          "end": 177.94,
          "en": "not from the dummy-data.js file anymore.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 177.94,
          "end": 180.15,
          "en": "We're past this world.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 180.15,
          "end": 182.2,
          "en": "Now we have the Firebase backend",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 182.2,
          "end": 184.88,
          "en": "and we wanna fetch that data from there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 184.88,
          "end": 189.31,
          "en": "Now, how do we fetch the featuredEvents from Firebase?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 189.31,
          "end": 192.37,
          "en": "Actually, when it comes to querying Firebase,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 192.37,
          "end": 195.43,
          "en": "you can adjust the HTTP request",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 195.43,
          "end": 198.6,
          "en": "which is being sent with some query parameters",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 198.6,
          "end": 201.49,
          "en": "to filter the data you are retrieving.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 201.49,
          "end": 205.25,
          "en": "If you search for Firebase realtime database filter,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 205.25,
          "end": 208.36,
          "en": "you'll find this retrieving data article,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 208.36,
          "end": 211.19,
          "en": "and there you'll learn how you can adjust",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 211.19,
          "end": 214.39,
          "en": "to the URL to which you send the request,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 214.39,
          "end": 217.44,
          "en": "with query parameters QL,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 217.44,
          "end": 220.26,
          "en": "filter the data which you are retrieving.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 220.26,
          "end": 222.88,
          "en": "And you can filter by a specific child keys,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 222.88,
          "end": 225.573,
          "en": "look for a certain values and so on.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 226.45,
          "end": 230.03,
          "en": "Now you can do that and feel free to dive into the docs",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 230.03,
          "end": 235.02,
          "en": "to implement it such that you do filter on Firebase side",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 235.02,
          "end": 237.89,
          "en": "for retrieving only selected data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 237.89,
          "end": 239.57,
          "en": "I will not do that here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 239.57,
          "end": 241.8,
          "en": "because this is not a Firebase course.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 241.8,
          "end": 244.53,
          "en": "And it's really just a dummy backend.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 244.53,
          "end": 247.38,
          "en": "Instead, I will add a new file here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 247.38,
          "end": 251.77,
          "en": "Let's say in a helpers folder,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 251.77,
          "end": 256.68,
          "en": "a file which I'll name api-util.js.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 256.68,
          "end": 258.44,
          "en": "So which has utility functions",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 258.44,
          "end": 261.22,
          "en": "for working with an API and in there,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 261.22,
          "end": 263.49,
          "en": "I will now add a function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 263.49,
          "end": 266.18,
          "en": "which gives me the featured events,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 266.18,
          "end": 269.43,
          "en": "but I will actually always fetch all events first",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 269.43,
          "end": 272.4,
          "en": "and then filter them just here in JavaScript",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 273.24,
          "end": 275.85,
          "en": "which is of course not ideal because it means",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 275.85,
          "end": 279.69,
          "en": "that we always fetch all the data, even if we don't need it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 279.69,
          "end": 282.76,
          "en": "But as I just said, that's just not the focus here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 282.76,
          "end": 285.1,
          "en": "it would be very Firebase specific",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 285.1,
          "end": 288.39,
          "en": "if we write the Firebase query logic here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 288.39,
          "end": 291.15999999999997,
          "en": "and that, well, basically leads nowhere.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 291.15999999999997,
          "end": 293.69,
          "en": "So therefore I'll go to dummy-data.js",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 293.69,
          "end": 298.61,
          "en": "and copy the getFeaturedEvents function from there",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 298.61,
          "end": 302.323,
          "en": "and add it here in the api-util.js file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 303.27,
          "end": 306.83,
          "en": "But I'll also add a number of functions here, getAllEvents.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 309.43,
          "end": 312.18,
          "en": "And in there, I will write the logic",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 312.18,
          "end": 316.57,
          "en": "for fetching all events data from Firebase.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 316.57,
          "end": 319.03,
          "en": "So I'll turn this into an async function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 319.03,
          "end": 321.68,
          "en": "so that I can use async await here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 321.68,
          "end": 323.72,
          "en": "I'll also convert getFeaturedEvents",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 323.72,
          "end": 325.7,
          "en": "into an async function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 325.7,
          "end": 330.7,
          "en": "And then here in getAllEvents, I will call fetch.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 331.61,
          "end": 334.07,
          "en": "So the built-in fetch API,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 334.07,
          "end": 336.06,
          "en": "which is available in the browser",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 336.06,
          "end": 340.26,
          "en": "and thanks to next JS also can be used inside",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 340.26,
          "end": 342.183,
          "en": "of getStaticProps and getServersideProps.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 343.96,
          "end": 348.94,
          "en": "And here, we'll then send a request to this Firebase URL.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 348.94,
          "end": 353.36,
          "en": "So to this rest API URL, which then triggers Firebase",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 353.36,
          "end": 356.11,
          "en": "to talk to our database here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 356.11,
          "end": 360.64,
          "en": "There we wanna reach out into the events node.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 360.64,
          "end": 362.91,
          "en": "So this node, which I added here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 363.97,
          "end": 365.71,
          "en": "and then because it's Firebase,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 365.71,
          "end": 368.33,
          "en": "we need to add .json at the end here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 368.33,
          "end": 370.293,
          "en": "That's Firebase specific.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 371.25,
          "end": 374.43,
          "en": "Now, since we use async here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 374.43,
          "end": 376.39,
          "en": "we can also await this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 376.39,
          "end": 380.163,
          "en": "to get our response like this without then.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 381.12,
          "end": 384.27,
          "en": "Under the hood, async awaits still uses then,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 384.27,
          "end": 385.52,
          "en": "but we can write it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 385.52,
          "end": 388.33,
          "en": "in this more convenient way here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 388.33,
          "end": 392.38,
          "en": "And we can get our data by awaiting response.json.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 394.47,
          "end": 397.93,
          "en": "We also might want to implement error handling here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 397.93,
          "end": 400.4,
          "en": "but for the moment, I'll skip it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 400.4,
          "end": 402.46,
          "en": "Instead here, we then have the data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 402.46,
          "end": 404.68,
          "en": "And as you learned in the last section,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 404.68,
          "end": 408.29,
          "en": "Firebase returns your data as an object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 408.29,
          "end": 411.23,
          "en": "So I'll transform my events here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 411.23,
          "end": 413.55,
          "en": "I'll add them as an empty array",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 413.55,
          "end": 416.73,
          "en": "and then loop through my data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 416.73,
          "end": 418.93,
          "en": "So through all the keys and data,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 134,
          "start": 418.93,
